re board writes, so foreman board writes do not use the stale copy. The exposure is any other caller of the PATH binary (sibling projects boards, operator one-offs) running a build with neither the DF-6 knobs nor the BT-039 hygiene.\n6. Deliberately NOT re-done in this cycle: a manual re-copy of the binary. Two writers building and installing into a live board repo while its tick lane can build is how the dirty-mtime confusion (BT-039) recurs; the durable half is the verification + provenance step, which is this row.\nAC: (1) an install target or a documented install step that installs the RELEASED asset by tag and verifies sha256, so the deployed binary is reproducible from the tag and identifiable; (2) a stated verification probe (e.g. `boardctl version --json` expected value, or `go version -m`) in README/Development so drift is detectable at any time, not just during a release audit; (3) after the next release, a probe shows the deployed binary reporting the released tag with vcs.modified=false and a revision that is an ancestor of that tag — quote the probe output; (4) the next cycle that re-cuts a release notes whether the installed copy moved, so this class gets a signal instead of a rediscovery.", "created_at": "2026-09-21T13:07:08Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-25T22:49:49Z", "worker_status": "pending", "detail": {"fingerprint": "637955a0964ae5ed87a200d77bd0672ad6f13b57a2ff1a7a256398c5b864894a"}, "ts": null, "complexity": 2, "foreman_note": null, "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/boardctl-BT-042", "branch": "wt/BT-042", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "sessions": null, "completed_at": null, "capability_tags": ["deploy", "install", "stale"]}
+ {"id": "DF-BOARDCTL-8", "title": "Burndown renders 2 of 20 points on v0.1.7 — the DF-BOARDCTL-1 fix passes x-labels (window bounds) as the x array, so linePath draws a two-point stub and silently discards the real open series", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-09-22 (dogfood run, fleet/multi-board angle; release binary v0.1.7, checksum-verified).\nREPRO: boardctl -C . render -o /tmp/r.html (this repo board, 20-day burndown window).\nEVIDENCE: payload derived.burndown = {window:[2026-09-03, 2026-09-22] (2 bounds), open:[2,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,5,4,2,1,1,0,0,9,1,2,2] (20 values)}; template.go:714 calls chartLines(bd, [{days: d.burndown.window, values: d.burndown.open}...]) — window is [start,end], not per-day labels. chartLines derives xs from series[0].days (2 entries), and linePath (internal/render/template.go:348) loops xs.length, so the drawn path is M30.00 117.33 L452.00 132.67 — 2 of 20 points, verified by executing the report's own chartLines/linePath under node with a DOM stub. The 9-open spike and the whole real series never render. Worse than the v0.1.6 blank panel (DF-BOARDCTL-1): now the panel LOOKS correct — a plausible down-trending line instead of an obvious placeholder — while discarding 18 of 20 data points. Reproduced independently on a fresh Debian 13 bunker box from a fresh clone (burnup renders correctly: days is a real per-day array there).\nFIX DIRECTION: give BurndownSeries a real per-day labels array (mirror BurnupSeries.days, derive.go:41) and pass it at template.go:714 + the overlay site; add a payload-shape test asserting burndown.days.length === burndown.open.length (the missing gate this bug class keeps slipping through).", "created_at": "2026-09-22T13:58:05Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T06:22:56Z", "worker_status": "done", "detail": {"fingerprint": "95c5312ada5106c989bdc6061ad8e810ce628b1c5570557d28cffe3916f5a81c"}, "ts": null, "complexity": 3, "foreman_note": "Merged 9b96380, pushed. Post-merge full suite green on main tree. CI on merge push pending — record GREEN after gh verification next tick.", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/coding-hermes-boardctl-DF-BOARDCTL-8", "branch": "wt/DF-BOARDCTL-8", "commit_hash": "d4a2c1b", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "BurndownSeries gained Days (per-day labels); template passes d.burndown.days at both chart sites; payload-shape tests added; wave worker glm-5.3-flash@zai-glm, gitreins verdict 7c3f0968 PASS", "sessions": null, "completed_at": null, "capability_tags": []}
+ {"id": "DF-BOARDCTL-9", "title": "One spec-invalid line kills ALL reads of a board — 9 live fleet boards are unreadable to boardctl (helios 2347 rows, consensus 1338, ring-runner 33) and validate offers no repair path", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-09-22 (dogfood run: validate/doctor/stats across all 53 live fleet boards on this host).\nEVIDENCE: 53 boards scanned; 27 exit 1. 4 boards exit 2 outright (tasks.jsonl-only: helios 2372 lines, h3-sdk-go-foreman, h3-sdk-python-foreman, sdk-typescript). Of the exit-1 boards, NINE carry spec-invalid JSON lines (jq independent-confirmed parse errors): consensus 1338 bad lines (raw unescaped control chars + truncated rows, first at line 157/167), helios 2347 (raw newlines inside string values), ring-runner 33 (literal bunker banner pasted mid-row), crier/deepseek-dashboard/musterflow/speclang/task-router/h3-sdk-python-foreman 1-2 each. Any single bad line aborts the WHOLE read: consensus list/show/validate/stats all exit 1 on line 167 alone — 164 valid rows unreachable. The affected boards are exactly the legacy pretty-printed-generation boards, and their writers inject multi-line tool output raw.\nIMPACT: the fleet's own integrity tool cannot read ~10 of its 53 boards, and the operator has no next step — the error names the line but no path to recovery short of hand-editing JSON.\nFIX DIRECTION (two-part): (1) degrade-with-evidence mode for reads/validate (e.g. --skip-bad-lines: report per-line parse errors and summarize the REST of the board, exit 1, never silently); (2) a validate --repair that re-serializes salvageable rows (json-repair for truncated/unterminated-string rows) into tasks.rewritten.jsonl for operator review before any in-place write.", "created_at": "2026-09-22T13:58:05Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T06:22:56Z", "worker_status": "done", "detail": {"fingerprint": "be4139a4be9ca22ed1776a715e69f17bb607641c2cf1a9c0dceb1051b0fa2d11"}, "ts": null, "complexity": 3, "foreman_note": "Merged 1c54dbb, pushed. Post-merge full suite green on main tree; CI success on the merge push (both workflows). Live-verified with rebuilt ./bin/boardctl on /tmp/df9-verify fixture: stats --skip-bad-lines lists 2 rows + SKIPPED-LINES evidence + exit 1; default stats aborts exit 1; validate --repair writes review file, exit 0, tasks.jsonl byte-identical.", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/coding-hermes-boardctl-DF-BOARDCTL-9", "branch": "wt/DF-BOARDCTL-9", "commit_hash": "daf0f3f", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "--skip-bad-lines degrade-with-evidence mode (tolerant read, per-line evidence, exit 1 when skipped) + validate --repair writing tasks.rewritten.jsonl without touching tasks.jsonl; live-verified on a synthetic bad-line board: salvage 2/drop 1, default abort path unchanged; gitreins verdict aefdfbba PASS", "sessions": null, "completed_at": null, "capability_tags": []}
+ {"id": "DF-BOARDCTL-10", "title": "ID-recycled near-dupes: 6+ live boards carry many DISTINCT findings filed under ONE recycled id (asce QA-ASCE-1 x6) — validate flags the dupes and dedupe-board correctly refuses to collapse them, but no lane tool fixes the hygiene", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-09-22 (dogfood run, dedupe-board dry-run on live boards).\nEVIDENCE: asce board: id QA-ASCE-1 appears on 6 lines (97/105/112/118/119/124), each a DIFFERENT finding (different title AND reasoning: header-frozen, spawn-pool exhausted, port-range exhausted x2, bunker-dropped). Same pattern on ai_plays_poke (QA-AI-PLAYS-POKE-1..3 x4+), hivemind-work, dexdat-memory, speclang. dedupe-board dry-run on asce: groups=[] — CORRECT per the fingerprint definition (sha over normalized title+reasoning, which all differ), so the SG-126 one-shot is not the tool for this; but validate permanently errors (exit 1) on every such board and nothing else addresses it.\nROOT CAUSE: QA lanes re-used a fresh cycle-number instead of advancing the id (QA-ASCE-1, -2, -3 refiled every cycle).\nFIX DIRECTION: (a) lanes must always mint fresh ids (id-recycled = new finding under an old key); (b) boardctl: doctor already itemizes them — add an id-aware dedupe mode (keep earliest line per id, close later lines as superseded-by-earliest with their text preserved in the event log) OR a doctor --json machine output lanes can consume; (c) optionally: accept known-alias statuses (dispatched, closed) as read aliases so parked-heavy boards validate clean once ids are fixed.", "created_at": "2026-09-22T13:58:05Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-22T13:58:05Z", "worker_status": "pending", "detail": {"fingerprint": "9a02e51a7b1cea82be27d619c1a62105b2bde603d9d08d2d606aec0e2beada91"}, "ts": null, "complexity": 3, "foreman_note": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "sessions": null, "completed_at": null, "capability_tags": []}
